2	// which screen is current, how many times its files have changed, and how many
3	// pop-out windows are open. It lives on the server, in memory and on this
4	// machine only (plan: ground rule 5) - it describes the moment, not the design,
5	// so none of it is written to the folder.
6	//
7	// The person's changes (a page, a state, a size, Reset data, a pop-out) are
8	// announced on the design's channel as `design-changed`, and each design
9	// surface reloads itself when it hears it, so the windows stay in step
10	// without any of them holding state. The agent's (the design's files) are
11	// `files-changed`: only the design bar reloads, saying the page on show is
12	// behind, and the page loads them when the person asks (R-v2q).
